From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 02:30:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] net: phy: mediatek-ge-soc: support LED polarity on MT7988

The MT7988 PHY driver derives the polarity of LED0 from the bootstrap
register and hard-codes that of LED1 to what the reference board uses.
Boards that wire the LEDs differently end up with LEDs that are lit
while the port is down and dark while it is up, e.g. the LTC Velo7 Max,
on which LAN2's LED1 and LAN3's LED0 are inverted.

The register field is the same as on AN7581, so hook up
an7581_phy_led_polarity_set() for MT7988 too. phylib applies the
active-low/active-high properties of the LED nodes after the driver's
probe, so a polarity set in the device tree overrides the derived one,
and boards without these properties keep the current behaviour.

---
--- a/drivers/net/phy/mediatek/mtk-ge-soc.c
+++ b/drivers/net/phy/mediatek/mtk-ge-soc.c
@@ -1504,6 +1504,7 @@ static struct phy_driver mtk_socphy_driv
 		.led_hw_is_supported = mt798x_phy_led_hw_is_supported,
 		.led_hw_control_set = mt798x_phy_led_hw_control_set,
 		.led_hw_control_get = mt798x_phy_led_hw_control_get,
+		.led_polarity_set = an7581_phy_led_polarity_set,
 	},
 	{
 		PHY_ID_MATCH_EXACT(MTK_GPHY_ID_AN7581),
